  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Energy Access - RSS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this scale-up, UCT will focus on regular reporting, quality assurance, and collaboration on research, emphasizing three key pillars: People, Technology, and Partnerships.

Research under the People pillar will assess the program&apos;s impact on beneficiaries, particularly in relation to sustainable development goals (SDGs) and local systemic change. The Technology pillar will explore the innovation ecosystem, identifying barriers and opportunities related to energy storage, green grids, and sustainable business models for scalable energy access.

Lastly, the Partnerships pillar will analyze the types of collaborations that enhance TEA&apos;s impact, drawing lessons from previous projects to replicate successful strategies in other regions. UCT aims to generate insights that align with TEA&#x2019;s objectives, disseminating findings through knowledge outputs and peer-reviewed publications.</narrative>
  </description>
